    "title": "Evansville first responders roll out Crosswalk to Care program - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Young ,\n1 hours ago\nHENDERSON, Ky. (WEHT) — First responders in Evansville are rolling out a big change.\nIt’s aimed at helping people who call 911 with medical concerns that are not emergencies. It’s called Crosswalk to Care.\nIt connects callers with trained care navigators who can walk them through their next steps. When a call doesn’t require an emergency response dispatchers can connect someone to a primary care doctor or urgent care.\nOfficials say ambulances will still respond to any life‑threatening emergencies. The service is free and available to everyone including people without insurance.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
